WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.372
Flexbox is the easiest way to place items in a row or a column.

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:09.682
Set display flex on a container, and its children sit in a row.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:12.892
Gap adds even space between the items.

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:18.099
Justify content spreads items along the row, for example space between.

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:22.984
And flex wrap lets items move to the next line on small screens.

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:33.977
Before you move on, check: Make a row of three cards with display: flex. Add a gap between them. Centre them with justify-content. Let them wrap on small screens.

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:37.822
In the next lesson: Responsive layouts.
